#
# LF-lock the vendored native-app build tail. The EVO repo is developed on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true; a CRLF checkout of any of these breaks the
# container build (shebangs, Makefile recipes, linker scripts, the compiler
# wrapper). See the `windows-writes-break-container-scripts` memory.

*           text=auto eol=lf
*.c         text eol=lf
*.cc        text eol=lf
*.cpp       text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.hpp       text eol=lf
*.ld        text eol=lf
*.map       text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.sha256    text eol=lf
prospero-clang18 text eol=lf

# The generated shim is git-ignored, but be explicit if one is ever committed.
*.prx       binary
